From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 06:25:50 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] airoha: gate vendor initcalls on airoha,en7581 machine
 compatible

The cascade target boots MediaTek and Airoha boards from one kernel,
so these built-in initcalls also run on MediaTek hardware where the
Airoha ethernet driver never probes and glb_eth stays NULL.

Ungated, wifi_lo_init registers four netfilter LOCAL_IN/LOCAL_OUT
hooks in init_net, creates /proc/wifi_local_fastpath, installs the
force-to-CPU GRO and pingpong RCU hooks, and registers a kprobe on
tcp_recvmsg at boot on every board. arht_dynamic_ifc_init creates
/proc/dynamic_ifc and installs its pingpong and sock-in-use hooks,
reachable from the wifi_lo timeout path. None of that belongs on a
MediaTek board.

Decline to initialize unless the machine is airoha,en7581, returning
0 since these are built-in initcalls. arht_kprobe.o has no initcall
of its own; its boot-time exposure is only via wifi_lo_init, which is
gated here.

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/arht_dynamic_ifc.c |    4 ++++
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/arht_wifi_lo.c     |    4 ++++
 2 files changed, 8 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/arht_dynamic_ifc.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/arht_dynamic_ifc.c
@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@
 #include <linux/module.h>
 #include <linux/kernel.h>
 #include <linux/init.h>
+#include <linux/of.h>
 
 #if __has_include("airoha_function.h") && __has_include("arht_dynamic_ifc.h") && __has_include("arht_kprobe.h")
 #define ARHT_DIFC_FULL_SUPPORT 1
@@ -1101,6 +1102,9 @@ static int __init arht_dynamic_ifc_init(
 {
 	int i;
 
+	if (!of_machine_is_compatible("airoha,en7581"))
+		return 0;
+
 	df_proc_entry = proc_create("dynamic_ifc", 0644, NULL, &dynamic_ifc_fops);
 	if (!df_proc_entry) {
 		pr_err("arht_dynamic_ifc: failed to create proc entry\n");
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/arht_wifi_lo.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/arht_wifi_lo.c
@@ -17,6 +17,7 @@
 
 #include <linux/module.h>
 #include <linux/kernel.h>
+#include <linux/of.h>
 #include <linux/netdevice.h>
 #include <linux/etherdevice.h>
 #include <linux/ip.h>
@@ -1221,6 +1222,9 @@ static int __init wifi_lo_init(void)
 {
 	int ret;
 
+	if (!of_machine_is_compatible("airoha,en7581"))
+		return 0;
+
 	hash_init(wifi_lo_port_ht);
 	hash_init(wifi_lo_hash_ht);
 
